<title>UK: Labour pledges worker rights, no over-regulation.</title>
<headline>Labour pledges worker rights, no over-regulation.</headline>
<byline>Alan Raybould</byline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Labour Party will introduce minimum workplace rights for employees if it wins the forthcoming election, but it will not over-regulate the labour market and there will be no central role for the trades unions, a senior Labour politician said on Friday.</p>
